%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2f0b0c553be8edd4682e9180fdd13e37, type: 3}
  m_Name: I2Languages
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::I2.Loc.LanguageSourceAsset
  mSource:
    UserAgreesToHaveItOnTheScene: 0
    UserAgreesToHaveItInsideThePluginsFolder: 0
    GoogleLiveSyncIsUptoDate: 1
    mTerms:
    - Term: Accuse
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - Acusar
      - Accuse
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - 
      - 
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q0_Answer_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Conozco mejor a Se\xF1or Se\xF1ora. No porque hable m\xE1s\u2026 sino porque
        se le escapa menos. Eso dice mucho.\n\xBFA qui\xE9n no miro a los ojos? A
        Se\xF1or Oculo. Ir\xF3nico, ya lo s\xE9. Pero hay miradas que no son ventanas:
        son pozos. Y yo ya he visto demasiadas cosas reflejadas en superficies que
        no deber\xEDan reflejar nada."
      - "I know Mr. and Mrs. better. Not because he talks more\u2026 but because
        he lets less slip. That says a lot.\nWhose eyes do I avoid? Mr. Eye. Ironic,
        I know. But some gazes aren't windows: they're wells. And I've already seen
        too many things reflected in surfaces that shouldn't reflect anything."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q0_Answer_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Conozco mejor a Se\xF1or Tele. No porque hable mucho, sino porque cuando
        miente\u2026 lo hace para proteger a alguien, no para salirse con la suya.
        Eso se nota.\n\xBFA qui\xE9n no miro demasiado tiempo a los ojos? A Se\xF1or
        Oculo. Es raro: no es intimidaci\xF3n. Es\u2026 como si al sostenerle la
        mirada te estuvieras comprometiendo a algo sin haber le\xEDdo la letra peque\xF1a."
      - "I know Mr. Tele better. Not because he talks a lot, but because when he
        lies\u2026 he does it to protect someone, not to get his own way. You can
        tell.\nWho do I not look in the eyes for very long? Mr. Oculo. It's strange:
        it's not intimidation. It's\u2026 as if by holding his gaze you're committing
        to something without having read the fine print."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q0_Answer_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\u201CConozco mejor a Se\xF1or Tele. Es el \xFAnico que habla como si estuviera
        narrando algo para otra persona\u2026 y eso delata m\xE1s de lo que cree.\n\xBFA
        qui\xE9n no miro demasiado tiempo a los ojos? A Se\xF1or Cornudo. Porque
        no aparta la mirada cuando deber\xEDa. Y eso no es valent\xEDa: es costumbre."
      - "\u201CI know Mr. Tele better. He\u2019s the only one who talks as if he\u2019s
        narrating something for someone else\u2026 and that gives him away more than
        he thinks.\nWho do I not look in the eyes for very long? Mr. Cuckold. Because
        he doesn\u2019t look away when he should. And that\u2019s not bravery: it\u2019s
        habit.\u201D"
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q0_Answer_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Conozco mejor a Se\xF1or Se\xF1ora. Porque no habla para sonar bien: habla
        para no romperse. Eso lo reconozco.\n\xBFY a qui\xE9n no miro mucho a los
        ojos? A Se\xF1or Liebre. No s\xE9 explicarlo\u2026 con \xE9l es como si la
        mirada fuera un \u2018s\xED\u2019 sin querer. Como si, si te engancha un
        segundo de m\xE1s, luego te cueste recordar qui\xE9n empez\xF3 la conversaci\xF3n."
      - "I know Mr. and Mrs. better. Because he doesn't speak to sound good: he speaks
        to avoid breaking down. I admit that.\n\nAnd who do I not look in the eye
        much? Mr. Hare. I can't explain it\u2026 with him, it's like a look is an
        unintentional 'yes.' Like if you hold his gaze for even a second too long,
        you'll have trouble remembering who started the conversation."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q0_Answer_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Conozco mejor a Se\xF1or Escroto. Es de los m\xEDos: dice poco, pero cuando
        habla es para aterrizar las cosas.\n\xBFA qui\xE9n no miro mucho a los ojos?
        A Se\xF1or Cornudo. No porque imponga\u2026 sino porque cuando le sostienes
        la mirada parece que te est\xE1 midiendo, como si fueras peso en una barra."
      - "I know Mr. Scrotum better. He's one of us: he doesn't say much, but when
        he does, he really brings things down to earth.\nWho do I avoid looking in
        the eye much? Mr. Cuckold. Not because he's intimidating\u2026 but because
        when you hold his gaze, it's like he's measuring you, as if you were a weight
        on a barbell."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q0_Answer_5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Conozco mejor a Se\xF1or Liebre. Es f\xE1cil de leer: si est\xE1 tenso,
        se le nota en el cuerpo; si est\xE1 tranquilo, tambi\xE9n. No hay mucho teatro
        ah\xED.\n\xBFA qui\xE9n no me f\xEDo de mirar demasiado a los ojos? A Se\xF1or
        Se\xF1ora. No porque mienta\u2026 sino porque parece que siempre est\xE1
        midiendo qu\xE9 parte de la verdad puede soltar sin que se le caiga todo
        encima."
      - "I know Mr. Hare better. He's easy to read: if he's tense, you can see it
        in his body; if he's calm, you can see that too. There's not much acting
        involved.\nWho do I not trust enough to look in the eye? Mr. Madam. Not because
        he lies\u2026 but because he always seems to be measuring how much of the
        truth he can let slip without it all coming crashing down on him."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q10_Answer_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se\xF1or Tele dijo que no hab\xEDa salido del coche hasta que vosotros volvisteis\u2026
        pero yo escuch\xE9 pasos alrededor del maletero antes de que nadie abriera
        la puerta de la estaci\xF3n.\nY no, no eran mis pasos. Yo camino\u2026 distinto.\nO
        miente, o alguien camin\xF3 con sus pasos."
      - "Mr. Tele said he hadn't left the car until you returned\u2026 but I heard
        footsteps around the trunk before anyone opened the station door.\n\nAnd
        no, those weren't my footsteps. I walk\u2026 differently.\n\nEither he's
        lying, or someone else walked in his footsteps."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q10_Answer_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se\xF1or Escroto dijo que hab\xEDa ido todo el camino con la ventanilla
        cerrada porque \u2018le molesta el aire\u2019. Pero yo recuerdo perfectamente
        c\xF3mo se quej\xF3 del olor a gasolina con la ventanilla bajada.\nO mi memoria
        est\xE1 fallando\u2026 o su historia se est\xE1 ajustando sobre la marcha."
      - 'Mr. Scrotum said he drove the whole way with the window closed because "the
        air bothers him." But I clearly remember him complaining about the smell
        of gasoline with the window down.


        Either my memory is failing me...
        or his story is being adjusted as he goes along.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q10_Answer_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se\xF1or Se\xF1ora dijo que no hab\xEDa tocado su bolso en toda la parada.\nPero
        yo le vi\u2014y esto lo vi bien\u2014meter la mano y sacar algo peque\xF1o,
        r\xE1pido. Podr\xEDa ser la mu\xF1eca, podr\xEDa ser una nota\u2026 lo escondi\xF3
        en el libro como quien guarda un billete.\nPuede ser inocente. O puede ser
        control de da\xF1os."
      - "Sir/Madam, you said you hadn't touched your purse the entire time we were
        at the bus stop.\n\nBut I saw you\u2014and I saw this clearly\u2014reach
        in and pull out something small, quickly. It could have been your wrist,
        it could have been a note\u2026 you tucked it into your book like someone
        stashing a bill.\nIt could be innocent. Or it could be damage control."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q10_Answer_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se\xF1or Escroto dice que no le gusta la m\xFAsica, que le distrae.\nPero
        yo le vi mover el pie. Dos veces. En el mismo estribillo.\nEso no lo haces
        si no est\xE1s escuchando. O lo haces\u2026 si est\xE1s intentando parecer
        alguien que escucha."
      - 'Mr. Scrotum says he doesn''t like music, that it distracts him.


        But
        I saw him tap his foot. Twice. During the same chorus.

        You don''t
        do that if you''re not listening. Or you do it... if you''re trying to look
        like you''re listening.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q10_Answer_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se\xF1or Tele dijo que no se quit\xF3 el Walkman en todo el tramo largo\u2026
        pero yo le o\xED hablar claro durante una canci\xF3n. Y no fue un \u2018tarareo\u2019,
        fue una frase entera.\nO se lo quit\xF3, o alguien estaba hablando con su
        voz. Ninguna me gusta."
      - "Mr. Tele said he didn't take off his Walkman the entire time\u2026 but I
        heard him speaking clearly during one song. And it wasn't just humming, it
        was a whole sentence.\n\nEither he took it off, or someone was talking in
        his voice. I don't like either explanation."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q10_Answer_5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se\xF1or Cornudo habl\xF3 de \u2018un olor\u2019 en el coche antes de parar\u2026
        pero luego dijo que no hab\xEDa estado atento al trayecto, que iba a lo suyo.\n\xBFEn
        qu\xE9 quedamos? O est\xE1s atento a olores y detalles, o vas desconectado.
        Las dos a la vez suenan a historia retocada."
      - 'Mr. Cuckold mentioned a "smell" in the car before stopping... but then said
        he hadn''t been paying attention to the drive, that he was just minding his
        own business.

        So which is it? Either you''re paying attention to
        smells and details, or you''re completely disconnected. Both sounds like
        a fabricated story.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q11_Answer_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\xDAltimo en bajarse: Se\xF1or Escroto. Se qued\xF3 un segundo de m\xE1s,
        como si estuviera contando cabezas incluso antes de saber que hab\xEDa que
        contarlas.\nEl que m\xE1s tard\xF3 en volver\u2026 Se\xF1or Oculo. Y no por
        lento: por preciso.\nCuando alguien tarda por precisi\xF3n, es que est\xE1
        haciendo algo que no quiere improvisar."
      - "Last to get off: Mr. Scrotum. He lingered a second too long, as if he were
        counting heads even before he knew he had to count them.\nThe one who took
        the longest to return\u2026 Mr. Eyeball. And not because he was slow: because
        he was precise.\nWhen someone takes their time because of precision, it means
        they're doing something they don't want to improvise."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q11_Answer_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "El \xFAltimo en bajarse fue Se\xF1or Cornudo. Se qued\xF3 un segundo inm\xF3vil,
        como si estuviera escuchando algo dentro del coche antes de moverse.\nEl
        que m\xE1s tard\xF3 en volver\u2026 Se\xF1or Tele. No porque se entretuviera,
        sino porque volvi\xF3 mirando hacia atr\xE1s. Como si temiera que algo lo
        siguiera desde la puerta."
      - 'The last one to get out was Mr. Cuckold. He stood motionless for a second,
        as if he were listening to something inside the car, before moving.

        The
        one who took the longest to return was Mr. TV. Not because he was lingering,
        but because he kept looking back. As if he were afraid something was following
        him from the doorway.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q11_Answer_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\xDAltimo en bajarse: Se\xF1or Escroto. Estaba mirando el retrovisor como
        si esperara ver a alguien sentado detr\xE1s.\nY el que m\xE1s tard\xF3 en
        volver\u2026 Se\xF1or Cornudo. No tard\xF3 por despiste: tard\xF3 por decisi\xF3n.
        Como si hubiera ido a comprobar algo que no quer\xEDa que descubriesemos."
      - "Last to get off: Mr. Scrotum. He was staring in the rearview mirror as if
        he expected to see someone sitting behind him.\n\nAnd the one who took the
        longest to return\u2026 Mr. Cuckold. He wasn't late because he forgot: he
        was late by choice. As if he'd gone to check something he didn't want us
        to find out."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q11_Answer_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "El \xFAltimo en bajarse fue Se\xF1or Se\xF1ora. Se qued\xF3 un segundo con
        la mano en el bolso, como si contara algo sin mirarlo.\nEl que m\xE1s tard\xF3
        en volver\u2026 Se\xF1or Oculo. Y me dio mala espina porque volvi\xF3 con
        la cara de quien ya ha visto una escena\u2026 y est\xE1 decidiendo qu\xE9
        versi\xF3n contar."
      - 'The last one to get off was Mr. and Mrs. He stood there for a second with
        his hand in his bag, as if he were saying something without looking at it.

        The
        one who took the longest to return was Mr. Oculo. And he gave me a bad feeling
        because he came back with the face of someone who''s already seen a scene...
        and is deciding which version to tell.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q11_Answer_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "El \xFAltimo en bajarse fue Se\xF1or Oculo. Se qued\xF3 mirando por el cristal
        como si estuviera buscando un \xE1ngulo.\nEl que m\xE1s tard\xF3 en volver\u2026
        Se\xF1or Cornudo. Volvi\xF3 con calma, pero no era calma normal. Era la calma
        de alguien que ya hab\xEDa decidido qu\xE9 iba a decir."
      - "The last one to get out was Mr. Eyeball. He stared out the window as if
        searching for an angle.\nThe one who took the longest to return\u2026 Mr.
        Cuckold. He came back calmly, but it wasn't normal calm. It was the calm
        of someone who had already decided what he was going to say."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q11_Answer_5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "El \xFAltimo en bajarse fue Se\xF1or Tele. Se qued\xF3 trasteando con el
        Walkman como si le diera miedo que se quedara en silencio.\nEl que m\xE1s
        tard\xF3 en volver\u2026 Se\xF1or Oculo. Y no porque se perdiera: porque
        volvi\xF3 con esa cara de \u2018ya tengo una versi\xF3n\u2019."
      - "The last one to get off was Mr. TV. He stayed fiddling with his Walkman
        as if he were afraid it would go silent.\nThe one who took the longest to
        return\u2026 Mr. Eyecup. And not because he got lost: because he came back
        with that \u2018I\u2019ve got a version now\u2019 look on his face."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q1_Answer_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Oficial: necesitaba salir de la ciudad, aire, carretera, reset.\nReal: ven\xEDa
        siguiendo un rastro. No de gasolina. No de huellas. De ausencia."
      - 'Official: I needed to get out of the city, fresh air, open road, a reset.

        Real:
        I was following a trail. Not of gasoline. Not of footprints. Of absence.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q1_Answer_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Oficial: necesitaba despejarme, cambiar de aires.\nReal: me sub\xED porque
        no pod\xEDa quedarme sola con mis pensamientos. Y porque\u2026 a veces, cuando
        llevas un secreto en el bolso, necesitas movimiento para que no pese tanto.\nAdem\xE1s,
        me prometieron que habr\xEDa tiempo para leer. Mentira bonita."
      - "Official: I needed to clear my head, get some fresh air.\nReal: I got on
        because I couldn't stay alone with my thoughts. And because\u2026 sometimes,
        when you're carrying a secret in your bag, you need movement so it doesn't
        weigh you down so much.\nBesides, they promised me there would be time to
        read. A pretty lie."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q1_Answer_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "La raz\xF3n oficial, necesitaba material. Fotos, v\xEDdeo, recuerdos. Me
        apetec\xEDa documentar una escapada.\nLa real, iba siguiendo un patr\xF3n.
        Carreteras secundarias, estaciones de servicio aisladas, gente cansada\u2026
        Es un tipo de escenario que se repite en ciertos\u2026 incidentes.\nY porque,
        si algo sale mal, prefiero estar detr\xE1s de una lente. Pone distancia."
      - "The official reason: I needed material. Photos, video, memories. I felt
        like documenting a getaway.\nThe real reason followed a pattern. Back roads,
        isolated gas stations, tired people\u2026 It's a type of scenario that repeats
        itself in certain\u2026 incidents.\nAnd because, if something goes wrong,
        I prefer to be behind a lens. It creates distance."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q1_Answer_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Lo que le dije al grupo fue simple: \u2018me ven\xEDa bien acompa\xF1aros,
        tengo que estar en el mismo sitio que vosotros al final del trayecto\u2019.\nLo
        que no dije: yo no me sub\xED por el destino, me sub\xED por el sonido. En
        casa empec\xE9 a o\xEDr cosas donde no las hab\xEDa: un estribillo en el
        grifo, una voz en el ventilador, un golpe de bater\xEDa en la nevera.\nEn
        el coche, con el Walkman, al menos puedo poner una cinta y saber qu\xE9 parte
        es m\xFAsica\u2026 y qu\xE9 parte soy yo perdiendo el control."
      - "What I told the group was simple: \u201CIt would be good for me to join
        you; I have to be in the same place as you at the end of the journey.\u201D\n\nWhat
        I didn\u2019t say: I didn\u2019t get on board for the destination, I got
        on board for the sound. At home, I started hearing things that weren\u2019t
        there: a chorus in the tap, a voice in the fan, a drumbeat in the fridge.\n\nIn
        the car, with my Walkman, at least I can put on a tape and know what part
        is music\u2026 and what part is me losing control."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q1_Answer_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Me apunt\xE9 porque el plan ten\xEDa sentido: coche lleno, ruta corta, parar,
        llegar. Eso es lo que dije.\nLa verdad: \xFAltimamente no aguanto estar quieto.
        Si paro, pienso. Si pienso, me caliento. As\xED que prefiero moverme, entrenar,
        distraer el cuerpo para que la cabeza no mande.\nY s\xED, traje la mancuerna
        por eso. No es postureo: es\u2026 gesti\xF3n de da\xF1os."
      - "I signed up because the plan made sense: car full, short route, stop, arrive.
        That's what I said.\n\nThe truth is: lately I can't stand being still. If
        I stop, I think. If I think, I get worked up. So I prefer to move, train,
        distract my body so my mind doesn't take over.\n\nAnd yes, that's why I brought
        the dumbbell. It's not for show: it's\u2026 damage control."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q1_Answer_5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Me invitaron y dije que s\xED. Esa es la versi\xF3n socialmente aceptable.\nLa
        otra: me ven\xEDa bien estar rodeado de gente para no hacer una tonter\xEDa.
        Cuando est\xE1s solo, algunas ideas suenan razonables. En grupo, se te pasan.\nY
        s\xED, llevo la petaca por eso: no para hacerme el gracioso\u2026 para no
        irme del todo."
      - "They invited me, and I said yes. That's the socially acceptable version.\n\nThe
        other one: it was good for me to be surrounded by people so I wouldn't do
        something stupid. When you're alone, some ideas sound reasonable. In a group,
        they just slip your mind.\n\nAnd yes, that's why I'm carrying the hip flask:
        not to be funny\u2026 but so I don't completely disappear."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q2_Answer_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Yo\u2026 me desanud\xE9 del asiento trasero.\nEstaba tocando el cr\xE1neo
        con la yema de los dedos, como quien comprueba si un reloj sigue vivo. Y
        escuchando: el coche, cuando se para, hace un silencio que no es silencio\u2026
        es una boca cerr\xE1ndose."
      - "I\u2026 untied myself from the back seat.\n\nI was touching my skull with
        my fingertips, like someone checking if a clock is still working. And listening:
        when the car stops, there's a silence that isn't silence\u2026 it's a mouth
        closing."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q2_Answer_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Estaba con el libro de bolsillo abierto sobre las rodillas, pasando p\xE1ginas
        sin leer de verdad. Cuando me pongo nerviosa hago eso: hago como que avanzo.\nY
        la mu\xF1eca\u2026 la ten\xEDa en la mano, apretada. Como si fuera un ancla.
        No me mires as\xED: cada uno tiene sus man\xEDas."
      - "I was holding the paperback open on my knees, flipping through pages without
        really reading. When I get nervous, I do that: I pretend to make progress.\n\nAnd
        my wrist\u2026 I was clutching it tightly in my hand. Like it was an anchor.
        Don't look at me like that: everyone has their quirks."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q2_Answer_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Estaba limpiando las gafas. No por man\xEDa: por necesidad. Cuando el cristal
        est\xE1 sucio, el cerebro inventa bordes que no existen.\nY ten\xEDa la c\xE1mara
        preparada, sin grabar. Me qued\xE9 quieto escuchando el motor morir\u2026
        porque ese instante, justo antes de que todos reaccion\xE9is, es cuando la
        verdad suele asomar."
      - "I was cleaning my glasses. Not out of habit: out of necessity. When the
        lenses are dirty, the brain imagines edges that aren't there.\n\nAnd I had
        my camera ready, not recording. I stood still, listening to the engine die\u2026
        because that instant, just before everyone reacts, is when the truth usually
        emerges."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q2_Answer_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Ten\xEDa el Walkman puesto, con una cinta vieja. De esas que ya no suenan
        limpias, suenan\u2026 vividas.\nY justo cuando el coche se par\xF3, la cinta
        se comi\xF3 un segundo de canci\xF3n. Como si mordiera.\nMe lo quit\xE9 de
        golpe, como si el aparato me hubiera susurrado algo que no quer\xEDa o\xEDr."
      - 'I had my Walkman playing, with an old tape. One of those that doesn''t sound
        clean anymore, it sounds... lived-in.


        And just as the car stopped,
        the tape cut off a second of the song. Like it was biting into something.

        I
        yanked it out, as if the device had whispered something I didn''t want to
        hear.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q2_Answer_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Estaba apretando el mango de la raqueta. La llevaba en el regazo, como quien
        sujeta algo familiar.\nY con la otra mano hac\xEDa repeticiones lentas con
        la mancuerna, sin levantarla mucho, solo para no quedarme congelado. Cuando
        el coche se par\xF3, par\xE9 yo tambi\xE9n. De golpe. Eso no me pasa."
      - 'I was gripping the handle of the racket. I held it in my lap, like someone
        holding something familiar.


        And with my other hand, I did slow
        repetitions with the dumbbell, not lifting it very high, just so I wouldn''t
        freeze up. When the car stopped, I stopped too. Suddenly. That doesn''t happen
        to me.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q2_Answer_5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Miraba el retrovisor. No por paranoia, por costumbre.\nY estaba palpando
        la petaca en el bolsillo, como quien comprueba que lleva las llaves. No la
        saqu\xE9. Ni beb\xED. Solo\u2026 comprob\xE9 que estaba."
      - "I was looking in the rearview mirror. Not out of paranoia, just out of habit.\n\nAnd
        I was feeling for the flask in my pocket, like someone checking they have
        their keys. I didn't take it out. I didn't drink. I just\u2026 checked it
        was there."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q3_Answer_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Querr\xEDa hacerlo demasiado bien.\nUn humano no est\xE1 siempre en el tono
        correcto, ni responde a la velocidad correcta, ni mira donde \u2018toca\u2019.\nEl
        impostor no sabr\xE1 fallar con naturalidad. Y, sobre todo, no entender\xE1
        una cosa: los humanos se contradicen\u2026 y no lo notan."
      - "I'd want to do it too well.\nA human isn't always in the right tone, doesn't
        always respond at the right speed, and doesn't always look where they're
        supposed to.\nThe imposter won't know how to make mistakes naturally. And,
        above all, he won't understand one thing: humans contradict themselves\u2026
        and they don't even notice."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q3_Answer_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se olvidar\xEDa de lo in\xFAtil.\nUn humano guarda cosas sin sentido: tickets
        viejos, migas en el asiento, frases que no llevan a ninguna parte. Un impostor
        intentar\xEDa ser eficiente. Coherente. Demasiado limpio.\nY cuando le preguntes
        por un recuerdo peque\xF1o\u2014una tonter\xEDa\u2014te dar\xE1 una respuesta
        perfecta\u2026 que no huele a verdad."
      - "He'd forget the useless.\n\nA human keeps meaningless things: old tickets,
        crumbs on the seat, sentences that lead nowhere. An imposter would try to
        be efficient. Coherent. Too tidy.\n\nAnd when you ask him about a small memory\u2014something
        trivial\u2014he'll give you a perfect answer\u2026 that doesn't smell true."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q3_Answer_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se equivocar\xEDa en el ritmo.\nLos humanos dudan con microgestos, titubean,
        se contradicen sin que les importe. Un impostor imita la forma, pero no el
        tiempo.\nY fallar\xEDa en lo m\xE1s tonto: en c\xF3mo alguien sujeta un objeto
        \u2018propio\u2019. Si no te pertenecen tus cosas, se te nota en las manos."
      - 'They''d get the rhythm wrong.

        Humans hesitate with micro-gestures,
        waver, contradict themselves without a second thought. An imposter mimics
        form, but not timing.


        And they''d fail at the most basic thing:
        how someone holds an object that''s ''theirs''. If your things don''t belong
        to you, it shows in your hands.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q3_Answer_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Intentar\xEDa parecer coherente todo el rato. Y eso canta.\nUna persona
        normal mete la pata: se contradice, se corrige, se pone nerviosa por tonter\xEDas
        y a veces suelta una frase fuera de lugar.\nEl que est\xE1 fingiendo suele
        ir \u2018demasiado correcto\u2019: responde r\xE1pido, no duda, no se le
        escapa nada personal y evita detalles peque\xF1os que no puede comprobar
        (por ejemplo: qu\xE9 canci\xF3n sonaba, qui\xE9n habl\xF3 primero o qu\xE9
        asiento ocupaba)."
      - 'He''d try to appear consistent the whole time. And that''s obvious.

        A
        normal person makes mistakes: they contradict themselves, correct themselves,
        get flustered over trivial things, and sometimes blurt out an inappropriate
        remark. Someone who''s pretending is usually ''too proper'': they respond
        quickly, don''t hesitate, don''t let anything personal slip, and avoid small
        details they can''t verify (for example: what song was playing, who spoke
        first, or what seat they were sitting in).'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q3_Answer_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se notar\xEDa en el cuerpo.\nLa gente de verdad tiene h\xE1bitos: c\xF3mo
        se sienta, c\xF3mo se agacha, c\xF3mo reacciona a un susto. Un impostor puede
        clavar las frases, pero el cuerpo va tarde.\nY otra cosa: alguien que finge
        suele evitar cansarse. Nadie que est\xE9 actuando quiere sudar de verdad."
      - 'It would show in their body.

        Real people have habits: how they
        sit, how they bend over, how they react to a fright. An imposter might nail
        the lines, but their body is slow to react.


        And another thing:
        someone who''s faking it usually avoids getting tired. Nobody who''s acting
        wants to actually sweat.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q3_Answer_5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se pasar\xEDa de listo.\nIntentar\xEDa responder \u2018bien\u2019 en vez
        de responder \u2018normal\u2019. Dir\xEDa lo correcto, lo convincente, lo
        que encaja\u2026 y evitar\xEDa las cosas que hacemos todos: vacilar, cambiar
        de tema, quedarse en blanco, decir \u2018no s\xE9\u2019 sin verg\xFCenza.\nEl
        que finge quiere control. Y hoy, el control canta."
      - 'He''d try to be too clever.


        He''d try to answer "fine" instead
        of "normal." He''d say the right thing, the convincing thing, the thing that
        fits... and he''d avoid the things we all do: hesitate, change the subject,
        draw a blank, shamelessly say "I don''t know."

        The one who pretends
        wants control. And today, control is obvious.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q4_Answer_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "S\xED. Y la mayor\xEDa est\xE1n mal contadas a prop\xF3sito.\nTe dicen \u2018cambia
        de piel\u2019 para que busques costuras. Te dicen \u2018imita voces\u2019
        para que escuches acentos.\nPero lo peligroso no es lo que copia: es lo que
        borra. Un skinwalker convincente no se pone una m\xE1scara\u2026 te quita
        la tuya y hace que te parezca normal."
      - "Yes. And most of them are deliberately misrepresented.\nThey tell you to
        \"change your skin\" so you look for seams. They tell you to \"imitate voices\"
        so you listen for accents.\n\nBut the dangerous thing isn't what they copy:
        it's what they erase. A convincing skinwalker doesn't put on a mask\u2026
        they take yours off and make it seem normal."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q4_Answer_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "S\xED. Y siempre me parecieron cuentos para asustar alrededor de una fogata.\nPero
        tambi\xE9n he le\xEDdo versiones viejas, las que no suenan a pel\xEDcula.
        Ah\xED no hablan tanto de \u2018monstruos\u2019 como de confusi\xF3n. De
        no saber cu\xE1ndo empez\xF3 el enga\xF1o.\nEso es lo que me est\xE1 molestando
        hoy: que no s\xE9 en qu\xE9 minuto exacto dejamos de estar\u2026 normales."
      - 'Yes. And I always thought they were just scary stories to tell around a
        campfire.


        But I''ve also read older versions, the ones that don''t
        sound like movies. They don''t talk so much about ''monsters'' as about confusion.
        About not knowing when the deception began.


        That''s what''s bothering
        me today: that I don''t know at what exact moment we stopped being... normal.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q4_Answer_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Claro. En foros, en documentales malos, en conversaciones de madrugada.\nPero
        tambi\xE9n en testimonios que no buscan likes. La constante no es \u2018se
        transforman\u2019. La constante es: te convencen. Te colocan recuerdos como
        quien coloca fotos en un marco.\nY t\xFA firmas debajo sin leer."
      - 'Sure. In forums, in bad documentaries, in late-night conversations.


        But
        also in testimonials that aren''t seeking likes. The constant isn''t ''they
        transform.'' The constant is: they convince you. They place memories in your
        mind like someone putting photos in a frame.


        And you sign below
        without reading.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q4_Answer_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "S\xED, pero siempre contadas por gente que quer\xEDa hacerse la interesante.\nA
        m\xED me daba igual\u2026 hasta hoy.\nHoy lo que me da miedo no es \u2018que
        copie voces\u2019. Lo que me da miedo es que copie tu nostalgia. Que te d\xE9
        un recuerdo falso y t\xFA lo abraces porque te consuela."
      - "Yes, but always told by people who wanted to sound interesting.\n\nI didn't
        care\u2026 until today.\nWhat scares me today isn't that it will 'copy voices.'
        What scares me is that it will copy your nostalgia. That it will give you
        a false memory and you'll embrace it because it comforts you."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q4_Answer_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "S\xED, en v\xEDdeos y en charlas de bar. Siempre lo mismo: \u2018imitan\u2019,
        \u2018enga\xF1an\u2019, \u2018se ponen tu cara\u2019.\nYo no s\xE9 de mitos.
        Lo que s\xED s\xE9 es que, si esto va de enga\xF1ar, lo l\xF3gico es que
        no lo haga a lo bruto. Lo har\xE1 con detalles peque\xF1os. Con cosas que
        nadie discute."
      - 'Yes, in videos and in bar conversations. It''s always the same: ''they imitate,''
        ''they deceive,'' ''they impersonate you.''


        I don''t know about
        myths. What I do know is that, if this is about deception, it''s logical
        that they won''t do it blatantly. They''ll do it with small details. With
        things that no one questions.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q4_Answer_5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "S\xED. Historias y tonter\xEDas. La gente confunde \u2018miedo\u2019 con
        \u2018mitolog\xEDa\u2019 y lo mete todo en el mismo saco.\nPero te dir\xE9
        una cosa: aunque no existieran, el concepto funciona porque toca un nervio
        real. El miedo a que alguien est\xE9 contigo\u2026 y t\xFA seas el \xFAltimo
        en enterarte de qui\xE9n es."
      - "Yes. Stories and nonsense. People confuse 'fear' with 'mythology' and lump
        them all together.\n\nBut let me tell you something: even if they didn't
        exist, the concept works because it strikes a real nerve. The fear of someone
        being with you\u2026 and you being the last to find out who it is."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q5_Answer_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "La alpargata.\nUna sola. Suelta. Como si el par no existiera\u2026 o como
        si el otro pie hubiese decidido quedarse en otro sitio.\nY no me digas que
        \u2018se cay\xF3 de una bolsa\u2019. No huele a armario. Huele a tierra vieja.
        A caminata sin sombra."
      - "The espadrille.\nJust one. Lonely. As if the pair didn't exist\u2026 or
        as if the other foot had decided to stay somewhere else.\n\nAnd don't tell
        me it 'fell out of a bag.' It doesn't smell like a wardrobe. It smells like
        old earth. Like a walk without shade."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q5_Answer_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "La mu\xF1eca.\nY no, no porque sea \u2018rara\u2019. Es m\xEDa. La conozco.
        Pero\u2026 hoy la he visto en dos sitios distintos con muy poco tiempo entre
        medias.\nComo si alguien la hubiera movido para ver si yo me daba cuenta.
        O como si hubiera querido que yo me acordara de tenerla conmigo, aunque no
        lo estuviera."
      - "The doll.\n\nAnd no, not because it's 'weird'. It's mine. I know it. But\u2026
        today I saw it in two different places with very little time in between.\n\nAs
        if someone had moved it to see if I'd notice. Or as if they wanted me to
        remember having it with me, even though I wasn't."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q5_Answer_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "La c\xE1mara. La m\xEDa.\nPorque jurar\xEDa que la guard\xE9 en la mochila
        y, sin embargo, la encontr\xE9 en el asiento como si alguien la hubiera dejado
        ah\xED para que la viera.\nY si no es la m\xEDa\u2026 entonces es peor: significa
        que alguien sabe exactamente qu\xE9 modelo llevo y c\xF3mo la agarro."
      - "My camera. Because I could have sworn I put it in my backpack, and yet I
        found it on the seat as if someone had left it there for me to see.\n\nAnd
        if it's not mine\u2026 then it's worse: it means someone knows exactly what
        model I carry and how I hold it."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q5_Answer_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Una cinta que no es m\xEDa.\nNo me mires as\xED: yo s\xE9 cu\xE1les son
        mis cintas. Las etiquetas, las esquinas dobladas, el \u2018clic\u2019 al
        meterlas.\nPero hay una\u2026 sin etiqueta. Y juro que antes no estaba ah\xED.\nY
        si alguien la ha puesto, es porque quer\xEDa que yo le diera al play."
      - 'A tape that isn''t mine.


        Don''t look at me like that: I know which
        tapes are mine. The labels, the folded corners, the click when you put them
        in.


        But there''s one... without a label. And I swear it wasn''t
        there before.


        And if someone put it there, it''s because they wanted
        me to press play.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q5_Answer_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "La mancuerna.\nEs m\xEDa, vale, pero\u2026 jurar\xEDa que la dej\xE9 en
        el maletero al salir y luego apareci\xF3 otra vez en el asiento, como si
        nunca la hubiera movido.\nO estoy despistado, o alguien la recoloca para
        ver si reacciono. Y si es eso\u2026 mala se\xF1al."
      - "The dumbbell.\nIt's mine, okay, but\u2026 I could swear I left it in the
        trunk when I left, and then it reappeared on the seat, as if I'd never moved
        it.\nEither I'm absentminded, or someone's putting it back to see if I'll
        notice. And if that's the case\u2026 a bad sign."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q5_Answer_5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "La petaca.\nNo porque sea rara. Porque apareci\xF3 donde no la dejo. Yo
        la guardo siempre en el bolsillo interior, a la izquierda. Rutina.\nY al
        bajar del coche la not\xE9 en el derecho. O me la movieron\u2026 o alguien
        quiere que yo dude de m\xED. Las dos opciones son malas."
      - "The hip flask.\n\nNot because it's unusual. Because it appeared where I
        don't usually keep it. I always keep it in my inside left pocket. Routine.\n\nAnd
        when I got out of the car, I noticed it in my right pocket. Either someone
        moved it\u2026 or someone wants me to doubt myself. Both options are bad."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q6_Answer_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "S\xED. Hay tramos en los que recuerdo conversaciones\u2026 pero no recuerdo
        el paisaje.\nY hay tramos en los que recuerdo el paisaje\u2026 pero no recuerdo
        qui\xE9n iba hablando.\nEso no es cansancio. Eso es\u2026 edici\xF3n. Como
        si alguien hubiese cortado fotogramas del viaje y los hubiese pegado mal."
      - "Yes. There are stretches where I remember conversations\u2026 but I don't
        remember the scenery.\n\nAnd there are stretches where I remember the scenery\u2026
        but I don't remember who was talking.\nThat's not tiredness. That's\u2026
        editing. As if someone cut frames from the trip and spliced \u200B\u200Bthem
        together badly."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q6_Answer_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "S\xED. Hay un tramo en el que jurar\xEDa que estuvimos hablando durante
        media hora\u2026 y luego miro el reloj y han pasado siete minutos.\nY hay
        otro en el que deber\xEDa recordar algo\u2014una canci\xF3n, una parada,
        un cartel\u2014y tengo la mente\u2026 como cuando intentas recordar una palabra
        y solo te sale el hueco.\nEso me inquieta m\xE1s que cualquier historia de
        skinwalkers."
      - "Yes. There's a stretch where I could swear we were talking for half an hour\u2026
        and then I look at my watch and seven minutes have passed.\n\nAnd there's
        another where I should remember something\u2014a song, a bus stop, a sign\u2014and
        my mind is\u2026 like when you try to remember a word and all you can come
        up with is a blank space.\nThat worries me more than any story about skinwalkers."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q6_Answer_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "S\xED. Y lo not\xE9 de una forma muy simple: el contador de fotos.\nHay
        un salto. No enorme. Pero hay un tramo en el que deber\xEDa haber 12 o 13
        fotos\u2026 y hay 2. Y no recuerdo haber borrado nada.\nEso solo pasa por
        dos razones: o estoy fallando yo\u2026 o alguien est\xE1 editando el viaje
        en tiempo real."
      - "Yes. And I noticed it in a very simple way: the photo counter.\nThere's
        a jump. Not a huge one. But there's a section where there should be 12 or
        13 photos\u2026 and there are only 2. And I don't remember deleting anything.\nThat
        only happens for two reasons: either I'm doing something wrong\u2026 or someone
        is editing the trip in real time."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q6_Answer_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "S\xED. Te lo digo por algo muy tonto: la duraci\xF3n de la cinta.\nUna cara
        dura treinta minutos. Y yo la empec\xE9 antes de la \xFAltima salida\u2026
        y deber\xEDa haber terminado hace rato.\nPero cuando mir\xE9\u2026 iba por
        la mitad. Como si alguien hubiera rebobinado el mundo sin avisar."
      - "Yes. I'm telling you this because of something really silly: the length
        of the tape.\nIt's thirty minutes long. And I started watching it before
        the last exit\u2026 and I should have finished ages ago.\n\nBut when I checked\u2026
        I was only halfway through. Like someone had rewound the world without warning."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q6_Answer_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "S\xED. Por el cuerpo, otra vez.\nHay momentos en los que deber\xEDa estar
        cansado y estoy fresco. Y otros en los que me duele el antebrazo como si
        llevara una hora apretando el grip de la raqueta.\nEso no cuadra con una
        ruta normal. El cuerpo no se inventa fatiga as\xED porque s\xED."
      - 'Yes. It''s my body again.

        There are times when I should be tired
        but I''m fresh. And other times when my forearm aches as if I''d been gripping
        the racket for an hour.

        That doesn''t fit with a normal route. The
        body doesn''t just invent fatigue like that.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q6_Answer_5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "S\xED. Lo not\xE9 por conversaciones que se repitieron.\nNo \u2018parecidas\u2019:
        la misma frase, el mismo remate, como si alguien hubiera pulsado replay.
        Y lo peor es que nadie reaccion\xF3, como si fuera lo normal.\nEso no es
        cansancio. Eso es\u2026 algo raro."
      - "Yes. I noticed it because of the repeated conversations.\n\nNot just similar:
        the same phrase, the same punchline, as if someone had pressed replay. And
        the worst part is that no one reacted, as if it were normal.\nThat's not
        tiredness. That's\u2026 something strange."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q7_Answer_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Mi cr\xE1neo.\nNo por lo que es, sino por lo que pesa. No me refiero al
        peso f\xEDsico. Me refiero a que, cuando lo sostengo, me ordena la memoria.\nSin
        \xE9l, podr\xEDa jurarte cosas que siento verdaderas\u2026 y ser\xEDan mentira.
        Y eso es lo peor."
      - "My skull.\n\nNot for what it is, but for what it weighs. I don't mean physical
        weight. I mean that, when I hold it, it brings order to my memory.\n\nWithout
        it, I could swear to things I feel to be true\u2026 and they would be lies.
        And that's the worst part."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q7_Answer_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "El libro de bolsillo.\nPorque tiene marcas: una esquina doblada, una mancha,
        un subrayado que hice sin querer. Si alguien me lo cambiara por otro igual,
        yo lo notar\xEDa.\nY si yo lo notara\u2026 significar\xEDa que mi memoria
        todav\xEDa funciona. Ahora mismo eso ser\xEDa la \xFAnica prueba que me importa."
      - "The paperback.\n\nBecause it has marks: a folded corner, a stain, an underline
        I made by accident. If someone swapped it with another one just like it,
        I'd notice.\n\nAnd if I noticed\u2026 it would mean my memory still works.
        Right now, that would be the only proof that matters to me."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q7_Answer_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Mis gafas.\nSin ellas no veo bien y, lo m\xE1s importante, no puedo confirmar
        detalles. Si pierdo eso, me convierto en alguien que \u2018cree\u2019 en
        vez de alguien que \u2018sabe\u2019.\nY hoy\u2026 creer es un lujo peligroso."
      - "My glasses.\n\nWithout them, I can't see properly, and more importantly,
        I can't confirm details. If I lose them, I become someone who 'believes'
        instead of someone who 'knows'.\n\nAnd today\u2026 believing is a dangerous
        luxury."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q7_Answer_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - 'El Walkman.

        Porque no es solo un cacharro: es mi forma de demostrar
        que lo que digo tiene un ritmo, un orden.

        Si me lo quitas, me quedo
        con el ruido de fondo. Y el ruido de fondo es donde se esconde lo que miente.'
      - 'The Walkman.


        Because it''s not just a gadget: it''s my way of
        showing that what I say has a rhythm, an order.

        If you take it away,
        I''m left with background noise. And background noise is where lies hide.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q7_Answer_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "La raqueta.\nNo por sentimentalismo: porque tiene una marca en el marco
        y el cordaje est\xE1 tensado a mi gusto. Si me la cambias por otra, aunque
        sea igual, lo noto al primer agarre.\nSi hoy \u2018mi raqueta\u2019 no fuera
        mi raqueta\u2026 entonces ya no s\xE9 qu\xE9 es m\xEDo."
      - 'The racket.

        Not for sentimental reasons: because it has a mark
        on the frame and the strings are tensioned just the way I like them. If you
        swap it for another one, even if it''s the same, I''ll notice the difference
        the first time I pick it up.


        If today ''my racket'' weren''t my
        racket... then I wouldn''t know what was mine anymore.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q7_Answer_5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Mi petaca, siempre mi petaca.\nPorque es lo \xFAnico que tengo que s\xE9
        exactamente c\xF3mo pesa, c\xF3mo suena al moverla, c\xF3mo rasca la chapa.
        Si me dieran otra igual, la notar\xEDa.\nY hoy necesito una cosa que sea
        m\xEDa sin discusi\xF3n."
      - 'My hip flask, always my hip flask.


        Because it''s the only thing
        I own whose weight I know exactly, the sound it makes when I move it, the
        scraping of the metal. If someone gave me another one just like it, I''d
        notice the difference.


        And today I need something that''s mine,
        no question about it.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q8_Answer_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Un trozo de cuerda con un nudo espec\xEDfico. No es nada\u2026 hasta que
        sabes lo que significa.\nY tambi\xE9n llevo polvo en las u\xF1as. No es sangre,
        tranquilos. Es\u2026 ceniza antigua.\nSi alguien lo ve, empezar\xE1 a hacer
        preguntas que no quiero contestar porque las respuestas abren puertas."
      - 'A piece of rope with a specific knot. It''s nothing... until you know what
        it means.


        And I also have dust under my fingernails. It''s not
        blood, don''t worry. It''s... ancient ash.


        If someone sees it,
        they''ll start asking questions I don''t want to answer because the answers
        open doors.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q8_Answer_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Dentro del libro hay una nota. No es un mapa ni un conjuro ni nada emocionante.
        Es una frase escrita por alguien que ya no est\xE1 en mi vida.\nY tengo la
        mu\xF1eca porque era un regalo\u2026\nNo es ilegal. Es peor: es \xEDntimo."
      - "Inside the book there's a note. It's not a map or a spell or anything exciting.
        It's a sentence written by someone who's no longer in my life.\n\nAnd I have
        the doll because it was a gift\u2026 It's not illegal. It's worse: it's intimate."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q8_Answer_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Una tarjeta de memoria aparte.\nNo tiene imagenes picantes ni nada de eso.
        Son im\xE1genes de otra vez. De otro sitio. De gente que jurar\xEDa que no
        estaba all\xED\u2026 y estaba.\nSi la encontr\xE1is, vais a empezar a comparar.
        Y comparar es justo lo que hace que esto\u2026 se vuelva real."
      - "A separate memory card.\n\nIt doesn't have any racy pictures or anything
        like that. They're pictures from another time. From another place. Of people
        I'd swear weren't there\u2026 but were.\n\nIf you find it, you're going to
        start comparing. And comparing is exactly what makes this\u2026 real."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q8_Answer_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "En la tapa del Walkman, por dentro, hay una foto peque\xF1a doblada. No
        es nada criminal.\nPero es de alguien al que yo\u2026 no deber\xEDa seguir
        echando de menos.\nY si alguien la ve, va a entenderme demasiado r\xE1pido.
        Y eso me pone nervioso."
      - "Inside the Walkman cover, there's a small, folded photo. It's nothing criminal.\n\nBut
        it's of someone I\u2026 shouldn't still miss.\n\nAnd if someone sees it,
        they'll understand me too quickly. And that makes me nervous."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q8_Answer_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Una lista de tiempos y repeticiones que apunto en una nota. Suena rid\xEDculo,
        pero me obsesiono.\nY llevo una venda vieja en la mochila, de una lesi\xF3n
        que no deber\xEDa seguir doliendo.\nNo es ilegal. Es vergonzoso: significa
        que sigo compitiendo con cosas que ya pasaron."
      - 'A list of times and reps that I jot down on a note. It sounds ridiculous,
        but I''m obsessed.


        And I carry an old bandage in my backpack, from
        an injury that shouldn''t still hurt.

        It''s not illegal. It''s embarrassing:
        it means I''m still competing with things that are already in the past.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q8_Answer_5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Lo que hay dentro.\nNo te voy a decir qu\xE9 es, pero no es para compartir.
        Y no es por \u2018prohibido\u2019, es por lo que significa: es una muleta.\nSi
        alguien me la quita o me la juzga, me quedo\u2026 demasiado expuesto. Y no
        me apetece."
      - 'What''s inside.


        I''m not going to tell you what it is, but it''s
        not for sharing. And it''s not because it''s ''forbidden,'' it''s because
        of what it means: it''s a crutch.


        If someone takes it away from
        me or judges me for it, I''ll be... too exposed. And I don''t want that.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q9_Answer_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Un ciervo. O algo que quer\xEDa que yo pensara que era un ciervo.\nEstaba
        quieto, mir\xE1ndonos\u2026 y ten\xEDa esa calma de quien ya te ha visto
        llegar antes.\nLuego parpade\xE9 y no estaba. Pero el olor se qued\xF3. Ese
        olor\u2026 como a pelo mojado y hueso caliente."
      - "A deer. Or something it wanted me to think was a deer.\n\nIt stood still,
        watching us\u2026 and had that calmness of someone who's seen you coming
        before.\n\nThen I blinked and it was gone. But the scent lingered. That scent\u2026
        like wet fur and warm bone."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q9_Answer_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Un cartel. De estos cutres, de carretera secundaria. Lo vi dos veces.\nLa
        misma pintura desconchada, el mismo golpe en la esquina\u2026 y lo vi como
        si hubi\xE9ramos dado una vuelta enorme, pero sin haber girado.\nNo s\xE9
        explicar por qu\xE9, pero me dio la sensaci\xF3n de que la carretera estaba\u2026
        repiti\xE9ndose."
      - "A sign. One of those cheap ones, from a back road. I saw it twice.\nThe
        same chipped paint, the same dent in the corner\u2026 and it looked like
        we'd made a huge detour, but without actually turning.\nI can't explain why,
        but I got the feeling that the road was\u2026 repeating itself."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q9_Answer_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Un destello. Como un reflejo de un flash\u2026 pero yo no dispar\xE9.\nMir\xE9
        por el retrovisor y vi, durante un segundo, una figura al borde del arc\xE9n
        que parec\xEDa estar\u2026 posando. Quiet\xEDsima.\nCuando parpade\xE9 ya
        no estaba. Pero mi mano se fue a la c\xE1mara por instinto. Eso no me pasa
        con sombras normales."
      - "A flash. Like the reflection of a flash\u2026 but I didn't take the picture.\nI
        glanced in the rearview mirror and saw, for a split second, a figure at the
        edge of the shoulder that seemed to be\u2026 posing. Perfectly still.\nWhen
        I blinked, it was gone. But my hand instinctively reached for the camera.
        That doesn't happen to me with ordinary shadows."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q9_Answer_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Un coche parado en el arc\xE9n con las luces de emergencia.\nPero\u2026
        no vi a nadie alrededor. Y cuando pasamos, el coche estaba limpio, demasiado
        limpio, como reci\xE9n puesto ah\xED.\nY en mi cinta, justo entonces, se
        col\xF3 un susurro debajo de la m\xFAsica. No una palabra. Un aliento.\nPar\xE9
        la cinta. No quise comprobarlo."
      - "A car stopped on the shoulder with its hazard lights on.\n\nBut\u2026 I
        didn't see anyone around. And when we drove past, the car was clean, too
        clean, like it had just been parked there.\n\nAnd on my tape, right then,
        a whisper slipped in beneath the music. Not a word. A breath.\n\nI stopped
        the tape. I didn't want to check."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q9_Answer_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Un tipo corriendo por el arc\xE9n. Sin ropa reflectante, sin m\xF3vil, sin
        nada. Solo corriendo.\nIba a un ritmo imposible\u2026 y lo raro es que no
        parec\xEDa cansado.\nMir\xE9 dos segundos y, cuando volv\xED a mirar, ya
        no estaba. Ni delante ni detr\xE1s. Como si se lo hubiera tragado el borde
        de la carretera."
      - "A guy was running along the shoulder of the road. No reflective gear, no
        phone, nothing. Just running.\nHe was going at an impossible pace\u2026 and
        the strange thing is, he didn't seem tired. I looked for two seconds, and
        when I looked again, he was gone. Not in front of me, not behind me. As if
        he'd been swallowed up by the side of the road."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Answers/Q9_Answer_5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Un perro. O algo parecido a un perro.\nCruz\xF3 la carretera y no mir\xF3
        ni una vez al coche. Ni se asust\xF3. Ni corri\xF3. Fue\u2026 tranquilo.
        Demasiado.\nY cuando lo perd\xED de vista un segundo, no estaba. No hab\xEDa
        cuneta, no hab\xEDa campo. Solo desapareci\xF3."
      - "A dog. Or something like a dog.\n\nIt crossed the road and didn't even glance
        at the car. It wasn't scared. It didn't run. It was\u2026 calm. Too calm.\n\nAnd
        when I lost sight of it for a second, it was gone. There was no ditch, no
        field. It just vanished."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Characters/Character0Name
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se\xF1or Cornudo"
      - Mr Cornudo
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Characters/Character1Name
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se\xF1or Se\xF1ora"
      - "Mr Se\xF1ora"
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Characters/Character2Name
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se\xF1or Oculo"
      - Mr Oculo
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Characters/Character3Name
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se\xF1or Tele"
      - Mr Tele
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Characters/Character4Name
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se\xF1or Liebre"
      - Mr Liebre
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Characters/Character5Name
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Se\xF1or Escroto"
      - Mr Escroto
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: ConfirmAccusation_0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\xBFEst\xE1s seguro de que desas acusar a <style=Character>{[Character]}</style>
        con el \xEDtem <style=Item>{[Item]}</style>?"
      - Are you sure you want to accuse <style=Character>{[Character]}</style> with
        item <style=Item>{[Item]}</style> ?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: ConfirmAccusation_1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Si te equivocas algo malo ocurrir\xE1... \xBFseguro que queres continuar?"
      - If you make a mistake, something bad will happen... are you sure you want
        to continue?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: ConfirmAccusation_2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "No te veo muy seguro... Acusar a <style=Character>{[Character]}</style>...
        no s\xE9..."
      - You don't seem very confident... Accusing <style=Character>{[Character]}</style>...
        I don't know...
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: ConfirmAccusation_3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\xBFDe verdad crees que el <style=Item>{[Item]}</style> tiene algo que ver?"
      - Do you really think the <style=Item>{[Item]}</style> has anything to do with
        it?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: ConfirmAccusation_4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\xBFEst\xE1s seguro, seguro, SEGURO, SEGUR\xCDSIMO?"
      - Are you sure, sure, SURE, ABSOLUTELY SURE?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/AlpargataGuiltyDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "La suela no tiene desgaste normal: est\xE1 pulida en zonas imposibles, como
        si hubiese rozado piedra\u2026 o hueso. Por dentro hay pelos gruesos pegados
        al tejido y un olor met\xE1lico, a establo y ozono."
      - Description of a test item. This is just a description to see how the text
        looks when described.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/AlpargataName
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - Alpargata
      - Test Item
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/AlpargataNormalDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - Una alpargata vieja, algo gastada en la suela. Tiene tierra seca pegada y
        huele un poco a humedad, como si hubiese pasado horas en un maletero cerrado.
      - Description of a test item. This is just a description to see how the text
        looks when described.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/CamaraGuiltyDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Hay fotos dentro. En todas sale el grupo\u2026 y en varias aparece un sexto
        hueco: un espacio \u201Cocupado\u201D por un desenfoque con forma de persona.
        En una imagen, el flash ha captado algo peor: una cara que no es cara, pegada
        detr\xE1s de alguien, mirando a c\xE1mara desde donde no cabe nadie."
      - "There are photos inside. The group appears in all of them\u2026 and in several,
        a sixth space is visible: a space \u201Coccupied\u201D by a blurry, person-shaped
        object. In one image, the flash has captured something worse: a face that
        isn't a face, stuck behind someone, staring at the camera from where no one
        else could fit."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/CamaraName
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "C\xE1mara"
      - Camera
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/CamaraNormalDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Una c\xE1mara compacta con la tapa algo ara\xF1ada. Tiene una correa enrollada
        y est\xE1 llena de huellas, como si la hubiesen pasado de mano en mano."
      - A compact camera with a slightly scratched cover. It has a coiled strap and
        is covered in fingerprints, as if it had been passed from hand to hand.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/CraneoGuiltyDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "No es decorativo. Est\xE1 demasiado limpio en unas zonas y demasiado \u201Cfresco\u201D
        en otras, como si se hubiera lavado hace poco. Tiene dos perforaciones sim\xE9tricas
        arriba, como si algo hubiese intentado colocar\u2026 o retirar\u2026 cuernos.
        Cuando lo sostienes, notas una vibraci\xF3n m\xEDnima, como un zumbido que
        te sube por los dedos."
      - It's not decorative. It's too clean in some areas and too "fresh" in others,
        as if it had been recently washed. It has two symmetrical perforations at
        the top, as if someone had tried to attach... or remove... horns. When you
        hold it, you feel a slight vibration, like a buzzing sound that travels up
        your fingers.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/CraneoName
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Cr\xE1neo"
      - Skull
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/CraneoNormalDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Un cr\xE1neo peque\xF1o, blanqueado y seco. No tiene nada \u201Cfresco\u201D;
        da la sensaci\xF3n de ser un recuerdo raro o un objeto decorativo de mal
        gusto."
      - A small, bleached, and dry skull. There's nothing "fresh" about it; it gives
        the impression of being a strange souvenir or a tasteless decorative object.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/GafasGuiltyDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Los cristales est\xE1n limpios, demasiado: no reflejan igual que el vidrio,
        como si fueran una membrana tensa. Si las inclinas, ves un segundo reflejo
        con m\xE1s ojos de los que deber\xEDa haber. En la patilla interior hay una
        marca h\xFAmeda, reciente, como si alguien las \u201Csudara\u201D por dentro."
      - 'The lenses are clean, too clean: they don''t reflect like glass, as if they
        were a taut membrane. If you tilt them, you see a second reflection with
        more eyes than there should be. On the inner temple there''s a fresh, damp
        mark, as if someone had been sweating on them from the inside.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/GafasName
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - Gafas
      - Glasses
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/GafasNormalDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Unas gafas de ver con la montura algo rayada. Est\xE1n dobladas por una
        patilla, pero a\xFAn se pueden usar; parece que alguien las dej\xF3 con prisas."
      - A pair of eyeglasses with slightly scratched frames. One temple is bent,
        but they're still usable; it looks like someone left them in a hurry.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/LibroDeBolsilloGuiltyDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Las p\xE1ginas est\xE1n pegadas en varias zonas, no por humedad: por algo
        viscoso que se sec\xF3. Hay frases subrayadas con obsesi\xF3n, siempre las
        mismas: \u201Cser\u201D, \u201Cparecer\u201D, \u201Cimitar\u201D. En el lomo
        interior hay un pelo largo y oscuro\u2026 y no est\xE1 \u201Cca\xEDdo\u201D:
        est\xE1 prensado, como si lo hubieran guardado adrede."
      - "The pages are stuck together in several places, not from dampness, but from
        something viscous that dried. There are obsessively underlined phrases, always
        the same: \u201Cto be,\u201D \u201Cto seem,\u201D \u201Cto imitate.\u201D
        On the inside spine, there is a long, dark hair\u2026 and it isn\u2019t \u201Cfallen\u201D:
        it\u2019s pressed in, as if it had been deliberately stored there."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/LibroDeBolsilloName
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - Libro de bolsillo
      - Paperback
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/LibroDeBolsilloNormalDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Un libro peque\xF1o con las esquinas dobladas y algunas p\xE1ginas marcadas.
        La portada est\xE1 manoseada, como de haber viajado en una guantera."
      - A small book with folded corners and some marked pages. The cover is worn,
        as if it had been transported in a glove compartment.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/MancuernaGuiltyDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Pesa m\xE1s de lo que deber\xEDa: la gravedad parece \u201Ctirar\u201D de
        ella con mala leche. Tiene marcas de arrastre en el suelo\u2026 pero no rectas:
        curvas, como si alguien la moviera a cuatro patas. En el acero hay restos
        secos que no son \xF3xido: parecen gotas viejas de algo org\xE1nico."
      - "It weighs more than it should: gravity seems to be pulling it down with
        malice. There are drag marks on the floor\u2026 but not straight ones: curved,
        as if someone were moving it on all fours. On the steel there are dried remnants
        that aren't rust: they look like old drops of something organic."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/MancuernaName
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - Mancuerna
      - Dumbbell
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/MancuernaNormalDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Una mancuerna de hierro, pesada para su tama\xF1o. Est\xE1 oxidada en algunas
        zonas y deja un poquito de polvo met\xE1lico en los dedos al tocarla."
      - An iron dumbbell, heavy for its size. It's rusty in some areas and leaves
        a little metallic dust on your fingers when you touch it.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/MunecaGuiltyDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "La mu\xF1eca est\xE1 cosida con hilo que no deber\xEDa existir en una mu\xF1eca
        barata: parece sutura m\xE9dica. Al apretarla, no suena un pitido ni un cascabel:
        suena un \u201Cclic\u201D h\xFAmedo, como una articulaci\xF3n real. Y tiene
        algo dentro del ojo derecho: no es una lente\u2026 es como un ojo peque\xF1o,
        mir\xE1ndote de vuelta."
      - "The doll is sewn with thread that shouldn't be on a cheap doll: it looks
        like medical sutures. When you squeeze it, it doesn't make a squeak or a
        rattle: it makes a wet \"click,\" like a real joint. And there's something
        inside its right eye: it's not a lens\u2026 it's like a tiny eye, looking
        back at you."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/MunecaName
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Mu\xF1eca"
      - Doll
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/MunecaNormalDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Una mu\xF1eca de pl\xE1stico con la ropa sucia y el pelo enredado. Tiene
        una mirada fija bastante inquietante, pero en el fondo es \u201Csolo\u201D
        un juguete viejo."
      - A plastic doll with dirty clothes and tangled hair. It has a rather unsettling,
        fixed gaze, but deep down it's "just" an old toy.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/PetacaGuiltyDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "No huele a alcohol. Huele a algo dulce y rancio, como fermento vivo. La
        tapa est\xE1 caliente aunque el aire est\xE9 fr\xEDo, y el metal tiene microara\xF1azos
        por dentro, como si alguien hubiera bebido\u2026 con dientes. Si la agitas,
        el l\xEDquido no hace \u201Cchapoteo\u201D: hace un sonido espeso, como si
        tragara."
      - "It doesn't smell like alcohol. It smells sweet and rancid, like live fermentation.
        The lid is warm even though the air is cold, and the metal has micro-scratches
        on the inside, as if someone had been drinking from it\u2026 with their teeth.
        If you shake it, the liquid doesn't slosh; it makes a thick, gurgling sound,
        like it's swallowing."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/PetacaName
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - Petaca
      - Flask
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/PetacaNormalDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Una petaca met\xE1lica peque\xF1a, con un par de golpes. Est\xE1 vac\xEDa
        o casi vac\xEDa; al abrirla queda un olor fuerte, dif\xEDcil de identificar."
      - A small metal flask, with a couple of dents. It's empty or almost empty;
        when opened, it emits a strong, difficult-to-identify odor.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/RaquetaGuiltyDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "El cordaje no est\xE1 roto, est\xE1 mordisqueado. Entre las cuerdas hay
        pelusa blanca y fibras que no parecen de ropa\u2026 sino de pelaje. El mango
        tiene un agarre perfecto, demasiado perfecto: como si una mano \u201Caprendiese\u201D
        su forma a la fuerza, apretando hasta deformarlo."
      - 'The strings aren''t broken, they''re chewed up. Between the strands are
        white fluff and fibers that don''t look like clothing... but rather fur.
        The handle has a perfect grip, too perfect: as if a hand had "learned" its
        shape by force, squeezing until it was deformed.'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/RaquetaName
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - Raqueta
      - Racket
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/RaquetaNormalDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Una raqueta deportiva con el grip sudado y el cordaje algo flojo. No parece
        nueva, pero est\xE1 cuidada, como de alguien que la usa de vez en cuando."
      - A sports racket with a sweaty grip and slightly loose strings. It doesn't
        look new, but it's well-maintained, like someone who uses it occasionally.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/TestDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Descripci\xF3n de un \xEDtem de prueba. Esto es solo una descripci\xF3n
        para ver c\xF3mo queda el texto descriptivamente descrito."
      - Description of a test item. This is just a description to see how the text
        looks when described.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/TestName
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\xCDtem de prueba"
      - Test Item
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/WalkmanGuiltyDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "La cinta no tiene etiqueta, pero alguien ha escrito con u\xF1as: \u201CPLAY\u201D.
        Al darle, no suena m\xFAsica: suena una respiraci\xF3n, y entrecortada, una
        voz que repite nombres\u2026 y a veces se equivoca, como si estuviera practicando.
        Cuando lo paras, el motor tarda un segundo de m\xE1s en apagarse, como si
        algo siguiera girando dentro."
      - "The tape has no label, but someone has written \"PLAY\" on it with their
        fingernails. When you press it, there's no music: there's a sound of breathing,
        and a voice repeating names in short bursts\u2026 and sometimes making mistakes,
        as if it were practicing. When you stop it, the motor takes an extra second
        to shut off, as if something were still spinning inside."
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/WalkmanName
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - Walkman
      - Walkman
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Items/WalkmanNormalDescription
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - Un reproductor de casete antiguo con marcas de uso en los bordes. Si lo agitas
        suena algo dentro, como la cinta suelta o un muelle flojo.
      - An old cassette player with signs of wear around the edges. If you shake
        it, you can hear a rattling noise inside, like a loose tape or spring.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: No
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - Nope
      - Nope
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Questions/Question0
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\xBFA qui\xE9n conoces mejor del grupo\u2026 y a qui\xE9n no te f\xEDas
        de mirar demasiado tiempo a los ojos?"
      - "Who do you know best in the group\u2026 and who do you not trust to look
        into the eyes for too long?"
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Questions/Question1
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\xBFPor qu\xE9 te uniste al viaje? Dame la raz\xF3n \u201Coficial\u201D\u2026
        y la real."
      - Why did you join the trip? Give me the "official" reason... and the real
        one.
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Questions/Question10
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Si tuvieses que se\xF1alar una contradicci\xF3n que has notado hoy, \xBFcu\xE1l
        es y de qui\xE9n?"
      - If you had to point out a contradiction you noticed today, what is it and
        who is responsible for it?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Questions/Question11
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "A ver, dime una cosa: \xBFqui\xE9n fue el \xFAltimo en bajarse del coche
        y qui\xE9n tard\xF3 m\xE1s en volver?"
      - 'Okay, tell me something: who was the last to get out of the car and who
        took the longest to get back?'
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Questions/Question2
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\xBFQu\xE9 estabas haciendo exactamente cuando el coche se detuvo en esta
        estaci\xF3n de servicio?"
      - What exactly were you doing when the car stopped at this gas station?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Questions/Question3
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Si uno de nosotros no fuera quien dice ser, \xBFqu\xE9 error cometer\xEDa
        al intentar hacerse pasar por humano?"
      - If one of us were not who he claimed to be, what mistake would he make in
        trying to pass himself off as human?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Questions/Question4
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\xBFHas o\xEDdo historias de skinwalkers antes de hoy?"
      - Have you heard stories of skinwalkers before today?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Questions/Question5
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Estoy haciendo memoria\u2026 \xBFqu\xE9 objeto dir\xEDas que \u201Cno deber\xEDa
        estar aqu\xED\u201D y sin embargo est\xE1?"
      - I'm racking my brain... what object would you say "shouldn't be here" and
        yet it is?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Questions/Question6
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Oye, \xBFt\xFA tambi\xE9n notas que hay partes del trayecto que no encajan
        con el tiempo que ha pasado?"
      - Hey, do you also notice that there are parts of the journey that don't match
        the time that has passed?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Questions/Question7
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\xBFQu\xE9 objeto te faltar\xEDa si tuvieras que demostrar que dices la
        verdad?"
      - What object would you be missing if you had to prove that you are telling
        the truth?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Questions/Question8
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "\xBFQu\xE9 llevas encima que no quieres que nadie encuentre\u2026 aunque
        no sea \u201Cilegal\u201D?"
      - What are you carrying that you don't want anyone to find... even if it's
        not "illegal"?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
    - Term: Questions/Question9
      TermType: 0
      Description: 
      Languages:
      - "Antes de llegar aqu\xED, \xBFqu\xE9 fue lo \xFAltimo que viste en la carretera
        que te hizo pensar \u201Cesto no es normal\u201D?"
      - Before arriving here, what was the last thing you saw on the road that made
        you think "this is not normal"?
      Flags: 0000
      Languages_Touch: []
